title Fold O -- fill_table, and the family the queue could only half see
prompt Autonomous loop -- pick up the running thread, Standfast on reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, read one council-rota doc, sweep the prose Radiant, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md carries a closure note -- %81, %83, %84, %98, %110 all closed, and %73 is booked toward the chunking-storage horizon rather than open. The corrective queue is empty, so the constructive queue is honestly next.
think The running thread is unambiguous. The newest log's recommend line names fill_table as the next crux, ungated, and says fold M already widened it to public for exactly this. The printed queue agrees: fill_table 37 rungs x 69 lines = 2484 carried, largest standing.
think Council rota, lap index 1469 mod 27 = 11 -- active-designing/20260618-182412_single-stranded.md. Compose rather than braid, each part about one thing. A fold is that brief in its most literal form: one body standing free in the harness, reached by every rung that needs it, rather than forty-three braided copies each about the same one thing.
think Before folding I extracted every fill_table body in caravan/ and hashed them, rather than trusting the queue. Two families came back at sixty-nine lines: thirty-seven and six. The diff between them is one line -- pub fn versus fn. Forty-three rungs hold this body; the meter compares exact text and cannot see that.
think Fold M had already written the true number down -- 2,898 lines across forty-three rungs -- beside the four spine bodies it widened for this exact fold. So the tree knew, and the queue could not say. That is the finding worth keeping: a fold queue is a lead rather than a verdict, and it went into the scan's own header.
think Checked every reached symbol at column zero across all forty-three before a line moved. Eleven bodies and one shape needed pub -- 435 widenings. Every one exists in every rung; none had to be written, only published.
think One rung needed an import no other did. reclaim.rye predates the harness and never imported it. I read every module ladder_checks imports -- cohort, system, unhand, capabilities, cycle, carry, gap, boot, mask -- and none reaches back to reclaim, so the import opens no cycle. Its own witness proves it GREEN on metal rather than by that reasoning alone.
think mask.prefix_mask and mask.fence_after stay module-level in the harness rather than being reached through the rung, because a mask is the same arithmetic for every rung on the ladder. Reaching them through rung would have said something false about where that arithmetic lives.
obs The measured fall is 2,220 while the family itself gave back 2,173, and the 47-line difference is not noise. A declaration line is part of the body it opens, so publishing elder_waits in forty-three of the fifty-one rungs holding it split one family of fifty-one into one of forty-three and one of eight -- and a split lowers the carry by exactly one body, since the new family's first copy becomes a distinct text. Eleven such splits close the arithmetic. Nothing is estimated.
obs This fold prepared the next several the way fold M prepared this one. Every symbol widened leads a family still standing in the queue -- confer_one at 2,067 across forty, confer_slot at 1,638 across forty-three, start_one at 1,365 across forty. They are public now, and the ground for them is laid.
obs The delegate is sixteen lines rather than fold N's nine, because fill_table takes ten parameters where reckon_the_plan takes five. A fold shrinks a family to its call, and the call is as wide as the body's own seam.
obs No red was found this round, and the ledger is left exactly as it stands. Saying so plainly is part of Standfast: a lap that books nothing has an empty corrective queue, not an unexamined one.
loom fold=fill_table rungs=43 body_lines=69 delegate_lines=16 widenings=435 carried_before=2829 carried_after=656 ladder_carry_before=134809 ladder_carry_after=132589 ceiling_before=135000 ceiling_after=132700 disk_lines_before=373828 disk_lines_after=371654
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye fill_table lifted whole, reaching every symbol through the rung handed in; mask imported for the two module-level helpers
file caravan/reclaim.rye the one rung that needed the harness import, being older than the harness
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_carry_scan.sh ceiling 135000 -> 132700, and the fold-queue-is-a-lead caution seated in its header
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish re-pinned to the fresh measurement, closing prose repaired so no number stands unasserted
file caravan/README.md fold O section -- the split family, the 435 widenings, and the arithmetic that closes
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge rotated to fold O, fold N condensed to a pointer
recommend keep-going The queue names the next fold and its ground is already public from this lap: provision_notes leads at 2,093 across 24 rungs, with confer_one at 2,067 across 40 and confer_slot at 1,638 across 43 behind it. confer_slot is the better crux of the three -- forty-three rungs is the widest family standing, and every symbol a fold of it would reach was published this round. The one gate worth Keaton's eye stays small and unchanged: jinja2 and ply on the pier's Python environment open types.h, syscalls.h, bootinfo.h, faults.h, and the sel4.h umbrella in a single step, which is an environment change and so his word.
